'''Creeping Past Cacnea''' (Japanese: '''VS サボネア''' ''VS {{tt|Sabonea|Cacnea}}''), titled '''VS Cacnea''' in the [[Chuang Yi]] translation, is the 181st chapter of the [[Pokémon Adventures]] manga, and the first chapter of the {{MangaArc|Ruby & Sapphire}}.

It is subtitled '''A New Story''' (Japanese: '''新たなる物語''' ''A New Story'') in the [[VIZ Media]] translation and '''A New Story''' in the Chuang Yi translation.

==Plot==
{{spoilers}}
The story starts in the [[Hoenn]] region, where a wild {{p|Duskull}}, {{p|Volbeat}}, {{p|Beautifly}}, and {{p|Cacnea}} are seen attacking someone. The person opens a Poké Ball, and releases a Pokémon that easily defeats them without being seen. The person is revealed to be {{adv|Norman}}, the new [[Gym Leader]] of [[Petalburg City]], who is being interviewed by [[Gabby and Ty]].

Norman's wife watches as she drives a moving truck to her new home in Hoenn with her son in the back. She calls to her son that his father is on television, but guesses that he wouldn't want to see it in the first place. [[Inside of Truck|In the back of the truck]], a young man named {{adv|Ruby}} dolls up his three Pokémon: a {{p|Poochyena}} named [[Nana]], a {{p|Skitty}} named [[Kiki]], and a {{p|Ralts}} named [[Rara]].

Ruby notices that a piece of Nana's fur is too long compared to the other, so he cuts it to make both sides match. Suddenly, the truck gets stuck in the mud and comes to a screeching halt. [[Mom (Hoenn)|Ruby's mother]] tells him to come outside and help, but Ruby refuses due to the thought of his Pokémon getting dirty. 

Instead, Ruby opts for having Rara use her {{m|Confusion}} technique to move the truck out of the mud. Ruby opens the back of the truck to see Hoenn for the first time, where he considers it to be just like his Pokémon: beautiful.

==Major events==
* About two years have passed since the end of the {{MangaArc|Gold, Silver & Crystal}}.
* {{adv|Ruby}} moves from [[Johto]] to [[Littleroot Town]] in [[Hoenn]].

